From ab2d3ef182bfcc4d3d0874b9ec041a9d2ff72c91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:53:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 957/957] wifi: ath11k: clear CRASH_FLUSH only after recovery
 rebuilds the rings

ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() zeroes the ring state with
ath11k_hal_srng_clear() and then clears ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH. The
copy engine and data path rings are rebuilt only later, by
ath11k_ce_init_pipes() and ath11k_dp_alloc(). A WMI command issued in
between passes the CRASH_FLUSH check in ath11k_ce_send() and
dereferences the NULL tail pointer of the cleared ring:

  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 0
  pc : ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k]
  lr : ath11k_ce_send+0x114/0x350 [ath11k]
  Call trace:
   ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k] (P)
   ath11k_htc_send+0x188/0x3c8 [ath11k]
   ath11k_wmi_cmd_send+0xc8/0x2f4 [ath11k]
   ath11k_wmi_send_peer_create_cmd+0x78/0xe0 [ath11k]
   ath11k_peer_create+0x138/0x500 [ath11k]

Clear the flag in ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() once the rings are
rebuilt, before ath11k_core_start() sends the first HTC message.

Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1

Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261018210153.1925962-5-julius@bairaktaris.de/
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2439,6 +2439,8 @@ int ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(struc
 		goto err_firmware_stop;
 	}
 
+	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
+
 	if (ath11k_frame_mode == ATH11K_HW_TXRX_RAW)
 		set_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RAW_MODE, &ab->dev_flags);
 
@@ -2501,8 +2503,6 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_cr
 
 	ab->free_vdev_map = (1LL << (ab->num_radios * TARGET_NUM_VDEVS(ab))) - 1;
 
-	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
-
 	ret = ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
